21
00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.849
Yacov Manevich: Because, so I thought at first it would not work, because

22
00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:38.019
Yacov Manevich: When we sign anything, we concatenate the certificate that is used to verify the signature.

23
00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:42.419
Yacov Manevich: Hi, Angelina. Welcome. However…

24
00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:51.540
Yacov Manevich: In BFT, in order to minimize the… the storage, what we do is we don't actually use the certificate.

25
00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:56.339
Yacov Manevich: But we just use, the index of the certificate

26
00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.199
Yacov Manevich: In the, like, as part of the assigned data.

27
00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:13.340
Yacov Manevich: So, that's why this can actually work, because the index doesn't change. I mean, as long as the index doesn't change, and the public key remains the same, we… with this PR, we can actually

28
00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:23.479
Yacov Manevich: rotate a TLS certi… sorry, rotate a sign… an enrollment certificate of a RAF node without needed to do a config update.

29
00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:32.399
Yacov Manevich: And the nice thing about this is that we don't need to be… we don't need to make any kind of validation rule changes, such as…

30
00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:43.070
Yacov Manevich: capability changes, we just need the communication to work. So, most of what these commits do is actually take care of the communication part.

31
00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.840
